<h1>leaf</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A <a href="node.html"><em>node</em></a> in a <a href="tree.html"><em>tree</em></a> without any <a href="child.html"><em>children</em></a>. See the figure at <a href="tree.html"><em>tree</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Also known as</strong> external node, terminal node.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Aggregate parent</strong> (I am a part of or used in ...)<br>
<a href="tree.html"><em>tree</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="root.html"><em>root</em></a>, <a href="internalnode.html"><em>internal node</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
Every node in a tree is either a leaf or an internal node.  The root may be a leaf.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

